** Important git commands for VS Code:
################################################################
FOLLOW THIS ORDER 

git status - gets status on your stuff 
git switch -c {new branch name no spaces} - switch to branch 
git add {file names you want to add} or . - add file 
git commit -m "commit message" - commit the added file 
git push -u origin {file/ files you want to commit}

################################################################




1. Show the current state of your repository. i.e. What branch your on, changed files that haven't been staged, Staged files ready to commit, 



2. Commit your changes
git add .
git commit -m "Describe your changes"

    Stages your changes and saves them in your local Git history

3. Connect to a remote repository 
git remote add origin https://github.com/vasudevnair113/academylovesaim.git

    Links your local repository to one hosted on GitHub or another service. Usually done once.

4. Pull the latest changes
git pull origin main

    Downloads and integrates changes from the remote main branch
    To upload your commits, use git push origin main. Substitute your branch name if it isn’t main.


